Let me analyze this code change in context.

Based on my analysis, here's my review:

```json
{
  "summary": "Added Config import and changed hardcoded session title 'nezha-agent-session' to dynamic 'nezha-{agentId}' using Config.getInstance().getAgentId()",
  "learnings": [
    {
      "topic": "TypeScript best practices",
      "reminder": "When using template literals with Config values, verify the config value is guaranteed to be non-null/undefined. Check Config.validate() is called before using getAgentId()"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Testing",
      "reminder": "HttpTransport.doCreateSession() has no direct unit tests. Consider adding tests for session creation with mocked Config"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Code review",
      "reminder": "This change modifies SessionManager interface behavior - ensure any dependent services are aware of the new session title format"
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "type": "potential runtime error",
      "description": "If Config.validate() is not called before HttpTransport is used, getAgentId() could return undefined if neither sessionId nor config.agentId is set, resulting in session title 'nezha-undefined'"
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    "Add unit test for doCreateSession() that mocks Config.getInstance().getAgentId()",
    "Consider adding defensive check: const agentId = Config.getInstance().getAgentId() || 'default';",
    "The change looks good - using agentId makes sessions more identifiable in server logs/monitoring"
  ],
  "praise": "Clean, minimal change. Uses existing pattern consistent with other parts of codebase (HeartbeatService, Scheduler, etc.). Import path is correct.",
  "overallScore": 75,
  "codeQualityScore": 85,
  "testCoverageScore": 40,
  "documentationScore": 50
}
```

